# Foretrade settings for docker compose. scripts/setup.sh copies this file to .env and fills in
# the required values; edit .env, then run `docker compose up -d` again to apply. Never commit .env.
# Write one KEY=value per line, with no comment after the value. Wrap a value that contains $ in
# single quotes, or compose reads $ as a variable: ADMIN_PASSWORD='my$ecret-passphrase'.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required (scripts/setup.sh generates these)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres password, in hex because it goes inside a URL. It is fixed when the database volume is
# first created: changing it later locks the app out (reset with `docker compose down -v`, which
# deletes the data).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# 64 hex characters (32 bytes). Encrypts the API keys and the ChatGPT sign-in that the admin
# console stores. If it changes, stored keys can't be decrypted: re-enter them in Settings.
SECRET_KEY=
# The bootstrap admin: sign in to the admin console with these. Password: 12 characters or more.
ADMIN_EMAIL=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI model (optional here)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave AI_PROVIDER unset to choose the model in the admin console (Settings > AI provider).
# Setting it makes this file control the whole AI configuration, and the console shows it
# read-only. AI_MODEL, AI_BASE_URL, AI_API_KEY, AI_EFFORT and MODEL_KNOWLEDGE_CUTOFF are read
# only when AI_PROVIDER is set.
# Providers: openai, chatgpt, anthropic, bedrock, openrouter, gemini, groq, deepseek, xai,
# mistral, ollama, lmstudio, custom. chatgpt is set up by signing in from the console.
# AI_PROVIDER=
# The model id. Required unless the provider has a default (anthropic, bedrock, deepseek,
# mistral).
# AI_MODEL=
# Blank uses the provider's default. Required for custom (any OpenAI-compatible server, e.g. vLLM).
# Ollama and LM Studio on this machine default to http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1 and :1234/v1.
# On Linux they must listen beyond 127.0.0.1 for the container to reach them: start Ollama with
# OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0 (in LM Studio, turn on serving on the local network), and firewall the
# port if the machine is reachable from the internet.
# AI_BASE_URL=
# The key. A provider's own variable works too: OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY (or GOOGLE_API_KEY), GROQ_API_KEY, DEEPSEEK_API_KEY,
# XAI_API_KEY, MISTRAL_API_KEY.
# AI_API_KEY=
# Extended reasoning where the model supports it: on or off. Blank uses the provider's default.
# AI_EFFORT=
# Your model's training-data cutoff (YYYY-MM-DD). The backtest arena flags windows before it.
# MODEL_KNOWLEDGE_CUTOFF=2026-06-30
# Bedrock reads the standard AWS settings. In Docker, set AWS_REGION with AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID and
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY (or AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK) in this file; AWS_PROFILE needs ~/.aws
# mounted into the container.
# AWS_REGION=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web search and page reading (optional; the admin console can set these too, and wins)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Brave Search API key (https://brave.com/search/api/) for news and web search. Without one,
# search is off.
# BRAVE_API_KEY=
# A crawl4ai server that reads web pages, and its API token: both are required. Without them,
# pages are fetched directly.
# CRAWL_BASE=
# CRAWL_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ports and origins
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host ports. The web app is published on every interface; the admin console on 127.0.0.1 only.
# WEB_PORT=8080
# ADMIN_PORT=8081
# The browser origins the API accepts: every origin you open the app or the console on, the
# console's included. The defaults cover localhost and 127.0.0.1 on the ports above, so you can
# sign in only there. To open the app at any other host (a server's IP, a domain), list that URL
# and keep the console's localhost entries (e.g. http://203.0.113.5:8080,http://localhost:8081,
# http://127.0.0.1:8081 as one value), and set APP_URL to it.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8080,http://127.0.0.1:8080,http://localhost:8081,http://127.0.0.1:8081
# The admin console's origins: the only ones its API answers.
# ADMIN_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8081,http://127.0.0.1:8081
# The web app's public URL, for links in notifications and the console's link to the app (that one
# is built into the image: run `docker compose up -d --build` after changing it).
# APP_URL=http://localhost:8080
# true once the app is served over https.
# COOKIE_SECURE=false
# The image tag to run (a release such as 1.2.0, or latest).
# APP_VERSION=latest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Features
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI credits per user per day (the admin console can override them per user).
# AI_DAILY_CREDITS=500
# The live arena: AI agents trading a shared paper desk around the clock. It calls the model on
# a schedule, so it is off unless you turn it on.
# LIVE_ARENA=on
# A demo investor account, created at boot.
# DEMO_EMAIL=
# DEMO_PASSWORD=
# Real-time quotes for Asian exchanges, read from public exchange and portal feeds (comma-separated:
# krx, hkex, hose, sgx, twse). Off by default: check each source's terms before you turn one on.
# Without them, those stocks use delayed Yahoo Finance quotes.
# QUOTES_REALTIME=
# Notification emails through Amazon SES (needs AWS credentials and AWS_REGION), e.g.
# Foretrade <alerts@example.com>.
# NOTIFY_EMAIL_FROM=
